## Context

The Exp2 FP audit (`docs/fp-audit-exp2.md`,
`experiments/derived/exp2_fp_classified.csv`) flagged **48 distinct plants /
95 FP occurrences** as `reference_hole`: real Vietnamese thermal plants > 30 MWe
that no model could match because they are absent from
`data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` under any spelling, and recur across
multiple models (so they are not hallucination).

High-confidence additions (sum of appearances):
- **Kiên Lương 1 / 2 / 3** (23×) — Kiên Giang, coal, cancelled (~4400 MW
  complex); distinct from the existing "TBKHH Kiên Giang I, II" gas entry.
- **Hòa Phát Dung Quất** captive power (13×) — Quảng Ngãi, BFG/coal, operating.
- **Rạng Đông** (6×) — Nam Định, coal, proposed/cancelled.
- **Kim Sơn** (5×) — Ninh Bình, LNG/coal, proposed.
- **Yên Hưng** (4×) — Quảng Ninh, LNG, planned (PDP8).

Triage candidates from `statistical_borderline` (sum ≥ 2×), verify before
adding: `Cẩm Thanh` (likely the existing "Cong Thanh"? — may be a dedup, not an
add), `Bảo Đại`, `Cái Lân`, `Lục Nam`, `Vedan` cogeneration.

**Explicitly do NOT add** (out of scope, from the audit's `other` bucket):
`Ninh Thuận 1/2` (nuclear, not thermal-fossil), `Đạm Phú Mỹ` (21 MW),
`Bourbon` (24 MW) — both below the 30 MWe threshold.

## Why needs-human / Blocked-by 0394

Each plant must be sourced against primary documents (PDP7/7A/8 annexes in
`data/rag_corpus/`, EVN reports, GEM) before entering the reference — a manual
compilation step matching `PROVENANCE.md`'s single-author method. This builds on
the cleaned v2 file from 0394 so there is one version bump, not two.

## Approach
1. For each high-confidence plant, locate a primary source in `data/rag_corpus/`
   or an EVN/GEM record; record name, province, fuel, capacity_mwe, status,
   units_included, and the source line.
2. Re-check each borderline candidate against the v2 reference first — some are
   dedup targets (existing row under a variant), not new plants.
3. Append rows to `vietnam_thermal_v2.csv`; extend `PROVENANCE.md` source
   inventory; update the status distribution counts in PROVENANCE.
4. Re-score Exp1–3 from existing outputs; the `reference_hole` occurrences in the
   re-run audit should fall to near zero for the added plants.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each added plant has a cited primary source in PROVENANCE
- [ ] Kiên Lương 1/2/3, Hòa Phát Dung Quất, Kim Sơn, Yên Hưng, Rạng Đông present
- [ ] Borderline candidates resolved as add / dedup / reject with a note each
- [ ] Nuclear and sub-30-MWe entries NOT added
- [ ] `experiments/scripts/fp_audit_exp2.py` re-run: `reference_hole` occurrences
      drop by ≥ 70%
- [ ] PROVENANCE status-distribution counts updated; `make check` passes

## First failing test
Extend `tests/test_reference_integrity.py`: assert the named high-confidence
plants resolve to exactly one reference row, and that no added plant is < 30 MWe.

## Out of scope
- Matcher changes (→ 0392 / 0393).
- Reference de-duplication and romanization (→ 0394, prerequisite).
- Re-running the models (re-scoring existing outputs suffices).

